            ["C_Usage"] = "MegaCopier — copying that survives power cuts\n\nUsage:\n  mcopy copy <source>... <destination-folder> [options]\n  mcopy move <source>... <destination-folder> [options]   Move (instant on the same disk)\n  mcopy send <source>... <destination-folder> [--verify] [--move] [--also <other-folder>]... [--at HH:mm]\n                              Hand the transfer to the MegaCopier app (window and tray)\n  mcopy send --test <checksums|folder>...      Check checksum files in the app\n  mcopy send --delete [--secure] <path>...     Delete (securely) from the app\n  mcopy send --hash <folder|files>...          Create a checksum file in the app\n  mcopy send ... [--mirror|--update-only|--folders-only] [--dry-run]\n  mcopy test <checksums|folder>...   Check .sha256, .md5, .sfv, .xxh3... without the app\n  mcopy decrypt <encrypted|folder>... <destination-folder>   Decrypt .mcenc files\n  mcopy delete [--secure] --yes <path>...   Delete without the app (--secure: overwrite first)\n  mcopy resume [id]      Continue interrupted jobs (or just one)\n  mcopy jobs             List pending jobs\n\nOptions for copy:\n  --verify               Re-read the destination without cache, compare hashes and repair damaged blocks\n  --conflict <mode>      overwrite (default) | skip | newer | rename | fail | ask\n  --limit-mb <n>         Limit the speed to n MB/s\n  --force                Copy even if the destination is identical\n  --chunk-mb <n>         How often (in MB) progress is committed to disk (default 64)\n  --block-mb <n>         Size of each read/write in MB\n  --queue <n>            Simultaneous reads and writes in flight\n  --no-unbuffered        Use the Windows cache instead of direct I/O\n  --mirror               Sync: remove from the destination what is no longer in the source\n  --update-only          Only update files that already exist in the destination\n  --folders-only         Only create the folder structure\n  --dry-run              Simulate: say what would happen to each file without changing anything\n  --versions <folder>    Keep replaced or removed files in that destination folder\n  --skip-junk            Skip Thumbs.db, desktop.ini, .DS_Store, ~$...\n  --smb-compress         Ask for SMB compression when copying over the network (slow networks)\n  --atomic               All or nothing: the folder only appears when it is complete\n  --rescue               Rescue mode: save what is readable from a damaged disk (unreadable parts as zeros)\n  --delta                When replacing large files, write only the blocks that changed\n  --organize             Organize photos and videos into year-month folders by capture date\n  --skip-duplicates      Do not copy what is already in the destination (same content, any name)\n  --encrypt              Encrypted copy with a password (AES-256, .mcenc files)\n  --backup             Backup mode: bypass permissions (administrator console)\n  --crash-after-mb <n>   [test] Kill the process after confirming n MB of a file\n\nCtrl+C pauses the transfer; 'resume' continues from the last confirmed block.",
